# Explicit Wikipedia lookups. Every template is anchored to the
# "wiki"/"wikipedia" keyword, so the open {query} slot only binds inside an
# unambiguous request for an encyclopedia article and cannot swallow
# utterances a dedicated skill (weather, time, ...) should own. Open-ended
# "what is X" / "who is X" phrasings are intentionally NOT listed here; they
# are handled by the common_query fallback, which scores low and yields to
# any skill with a better answer.
can you find {query} on (wiki|wikipedia)
check (wiki|wikipedia) for {query}
find details about {query} (on|in) (wiki|wikipedia)
give me information (on|about) {query} from (wiki|wikipedia)
look up {query} (on|in) (wiki|wikipedia)
search (wiki|wikipedia) for [details about] {query}
tell me about {query} (on|from) (wiki|wikipedia)
what does [the] (wiki|wikipedia) say (about|regarding) {query}
what is known about {query} on (wiki|wikipedia)
what is the (wiki|wikipedia) entry for {query}
what's on (wiki|wikipedia) about {query}
who (is|was) {query} (on|according to) (wiki|wikipedia)
(wiki|wikipedia) {query}
